227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (This paper presents Enterprise-LightRAG, an evolution of the LightRAG architecture designed for production-scale, high-throughput applications. By replacing volatile in-memory storage structures with a persistent Neo4j graph platform, we remove memory scalability bottlenecks. Integrating a Hybrid Lexical-Semantic Search Track with Reciprocal Rank Fusion ensures reliable retrieval paths, successfully bridging the lexical gap that often challenges standard vector-only pipelines. Furthermore, the introduction of an asynchronous execution model via Celery and Redis, alongside an inline token compression layer powered by LLMLingua, balances operational cost with system throughput. Supported by a rigorous evaluation methodology using Ragas, this architecture provides a scalable path for deploying graph-augmented generation systems within enterprise environments. 10. References)
/E (This paper presents Enterprise-LightRAG, an evolution of the LightRAG architecture designed for production-scale, high-throughput applications. By replacing volatile in-memory storage structures with a persistent Neo4j graph platform, we remove memory scalability bottlenecks. Integrating a Hybrid Lexical-Semantic Search Track with Reciprocal Rank Fusion ensures reliable retrieval paths, successfully bridging the lexical gap that often challenges standard vector-only pipelines. Furthermore, the introduction of an asynchronous execution model via Celery and Redis, alongside an inline token compression layer powered by LLMLingua, balances operational cost with system throughput. Supported by a rigorous evaluation methodology using Ragas, this architecture provides a scalable path for deploying graph-augmented generation systems within enterprise environments. 10. References)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
