483 0 obj
<<
/Title (Dynamic Synchronic Latency: Synchronizing updates across separate database engines \(Neo4j for graph topology and Qdrant/Milvus for vector spaces\) introduces minor transactional overhead during massive real-time ingestion streams. Dependence on Core Extractor Quality: The system's downstream retrieval accuracy remains dependent on the initial extraction capability of the ingestion model. If the extraction agent misses core relationships during chunk parsing, the underlying graph index will be incomplete. Cypher Query Structural Limits: Complex, multi-hop Cypher traversals spanning deeper execution boundaries \(e.g., greater than 4-hop lookups\) can lead to query timeouts if graph topologies become dense.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 416 0 R
>>
endobj
